Using Gate Pulse Propagation
Using the -xlrm gd_pulseprop option, VCS always propagates a gate pulse, even when
the pulse width is equal to the gate delay. For example, consider the following Verilog
code:
module dut(qout,dinA,dinB);
output qout;
input dinA;
input dinB;

xor #10 inst(qout,dinA,dinB);

