With an Active Specify Path
To enable delayed annotation, use +ignorempcond=match_min or
+ignorempcond=match_max when there is an active specify path.
Support for Delay Selection Options for Recent Active Paths by
Ignoring Condition Checking
VCS supports delayed annotations for recent active paths by ignoring condition checking
and inserting applicable delays based on delay selection options.
You can use the following runtime options for delay selections:
• +ignorempcond=match_max
VCS applies the maximum delay from the active paths.
• +ignorempcond=match_min
VCS applies the minimum delay from the active paths.
In the following example, both inputs A1 and A2 change simultaneously at time 500ns.
module test_d ;
reg A1,A2,B1;
wire Z;
AO22 u4 (.A1(A1),.A2(A2),.B1(B1),.Z(Z));

$monitor("Time:%t A1=%b, A2=%b, Z=%b",$realtime, A1,A2,Z);
end

$sdf_annotate ("dut.sdf",test_d,,,"MAXIMUM");
A1 = 1;
A2 = 1;
B1 = 1;
#500 A1 = 0; //Both A1 and A2 are changing simultaneously at time 500.
#500 A2 = 0;
#10000 $finish;
join

`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module AO22 (A1,A2,B1,Z);
input A1,A2,B1;
output Z;
and (Z,A1,A2);

