• Support for Initial Assignment of Nettypes Inside Package
• Support for Integral Types in String Concatenation

Unique/Priority Case/IF Final Semantic Enhancements (-xlrm
uniq_prior_final Compile-Time Option)
The behavior of the compliance checking keywords unique and priority for case and
for ifelse selection statements. This is defined in the Conditional if-else statement
Section 12.4. “Conditional if-else statement” in some cases can cause spurious warnings
when used inside a module's continuous assignment or always block. By default, VCS
evaluate compliance with unique or priority on every update to the selection statement
input.
VCS provides a -xlrm uniq_prior_final compile-time option. This option forces
unique and priority to evaluate compliance only on the stable and final value of the
selection input. The evaluation occurs at the end of a simulation timestep.

