Using Class Variable in std::randomize Call
Using Class Variable in std::randomize Call
VCS supports class variable in the std::randomize() call. You can call std::randomize
with class object variable. Consider the following test case:
Example 187 test.sv
class fs_array;
rand bit [3:0] array1[4];
rand bit [7:0] array2[6];

function void display();
$display("array1 = %p",array1);
$display("array2 = %p",array2);

program std_randomize;
bit [07:0] addr;
bit [31:0] data;
bit [63:0] data_x_4;

fs_array pkt;

pkt = new();
std::randomize(pkt);
pkt.display();
end

std::randomize(addr);
$display("Value of addr is %h",addr);
std::randomize(data,data_x_4) with { data == addr * 8;
data_x_4 == data * 4;
};
$display("Value of data is %0d",data);
$display("Value of data_x_4 is %0d",data_x_4);
end
