Support for Expression Evaluation to Integral Involving Real
Variables Inside $rose and $fell Sampled Functions
VCS supports expression evaluation to integral involving real variables inside the $rose
and $fell sampled functions. You must use the -xlrm real_in_rose_fell compile
option to enable this support. The following is the use model:
% vcs -sverilog <file_name> -xlrm real_in_rose_fell
The following is the example:
Example 250 test.sv
bit clk, a;
real b;
A1 : assert property (@(posedge clk) $rose(a) |-> $rose(b == 0));
#1 a = 1;
#5 b = 1; a = 0;
#5 a = 1;
#5 b = 0;
#20 $finish;
end
The following is the behavior without the -xlrm real_in_rose_fell option:

Error-[SVA-ETTNASSF] The expression is not permitted.
Expressions of real, time, string and event types, as well as dynamic
SystemVerilog types, are not allowed in sampled system functions.
