VHDL 2019: Support for Conditional Expressions
Starting with this release, VCS supports conditional expressions as specified in the VHDL
2019 Language Reference Model (LRM). The 2019 LRM takes the conditional syntax
similar to the one used in the conditional variable assignment statements. It allows the
conditional syntax in a place where the expression might be used, either directly in cases
where it has no significant impact on the grammar, or enclosed in parentheses elsewhere.
Conditional expressions can simplify declarations and expressions, such as declarations
for temporary values, or functions encapsulating an if statement, which might otherwise
require additional declarations. It is beneficial when the conditional expressions are
available in your designs or when you require them for incorporating IP.
To support conditional expressions, you must invoke the vhdlan command with the
-vhdl19 switch.

VHDL 2019: Support for Conditional Expressions
If the VHDL_MODE setup variable is set to 19 or VHDL19, VCS enables the VHDL 2019
constructs and the other supported values.
VCS supports conditional expressions at the following places:
• actual designator
• attribute specification
• constant declaration
• variable declaration
• signal declaration
• interface object declaration (static)
• statements (including unaffected)
◦ variable assignment
◦ force
◦ value return
• elsewhere (enclosed in parentheses)
h1 : filter(a, b, x * 10 when c < 5 else x * 20 when c < 10 else x *
100);

attribute filter_length of a : architecture is x * 10 when c < 5 else x *
20 when c < 10 else x * 100;

constant flen : integer := x * 10 when c < 5 else x * 20 when c < 10 else
x * 100;

function get_flen (base : integer; bmul : integer := x * 10 when c < 5
else x * 20 when c < 10 else x * 100) return integer;

function get_flen(x, c : integer) return integer is
variable i : natural;
v
return x * -3 when c < 0 else unaffected;
for i in 0 to 100 loop
return x * b when i >= c; -- implicit else unaffected
b := a + b;
a := b - a;
i := i + 1;
-- error if b < a is false, function returns without value
return 0 when b < a;

