Discontinued -ipkey Option
The -ipkey key option will be obsolete in future releases.
IP providers should use -ipprotect instead. It allows you to specify various protection
pragmas (via a protection header file) which are needed while generating interoperably
encrypted IPs.
VCS will no longer use the key you pass with the -ipkey key option. It will generate a
secure key internally.

VCS supports the encryption and decryption of the VHDL IP source code in protection
envelopes, as defined by the IEEE VHDL Standard 1076-2008.
