Support for VHDL 2008 Enhanced Generics in Components
VCS supports the usage of VHDL 2008 enhanced generics (types/subprograms/
packages) in components and corresponding instantiations of components with generic
maps as defined in the VHDL 2008 LRM.
With this support of enhanced generics in VHDL 2008, you can declare generic types,
sub-programs, and packages in a component. This allows you to declare abstract and
reusable entities with different types and design specialization. When you instantiate a
component, you supply values for the generic constants for that instance.
Following is the use model to enable this feature:
% vhdlan -vhdl08 <other_options> file.vhd

The following example shows the usage of generic type and function in component
interface:
Example 291 test.vhd
entity GenericCnt is
generic (
type T;
Constant C : T;
function GenFunc (signal arg : T) return T
);
clk : in bit;
rst : in bit;
Cnt : inout T
);

architecture arch of GenericCnt is
process(clk,rst)
if(rst='1') then
cnt <= C;
elsif(clk'event and clk='1') then
cnt <= GenFunc(cnt);

use ieee.std_logic_unsigned.all;
use ieee.std_logic_arith.all;

component GenericCnt is
type T;
Constant C : T;
function GenFunc(signal arg : T) return T
);
clk : in bit;
rst : in bit;
Cnt : inout T
);

signal clk , rst : bit;
signal cnt : std_logic_vector(2 downto 0):= (others => '0');
function IncrCnt ( signal arg : in std_logic_vector ) return
std_logic_vector is
return arg + 1;
end function;
inst : GenericCnt generic map(
T => std_logic_vector(2 downto 0),
C => (others => '0'),
GenFunc => IncrCnt
)
port map ( clk,rst,cnt);
if(now = 80 ns) then
clk <= '0';
clk <= '1';

rst <= '1';
wait for 3 ns;
rst <= '0';

process(cnt)
write(l,"time : " & time'image(now));
write(l," CNT : " & integer'image(conv_integer(unsigned(cnt))));
