Support for Wildcard Character and the -exclude Option in the
Mixed Signal Control Command
The
-exclude
-exclude option is supported in the use_verilog mixed signal control command,
which can be used to provide the instances that must not be partitioned. Also, the "*"
wildcard character is supported in the hierarchical path of the -inst and -exclude options
in the use_verilog mixed signal control command. This feature is useful when there are
large number of instances in the design.

Support for Wildcard Character and the -exclude Option in the Mixed Signal Control
Command
The syntax of the -exclude option with the wildcard character is as follows:
use_verilog -module inverter -inst top.*.* -exclude top.a0.*;
The "*" wildcard character in the instance name is only supported if the
-adopt wildcard
-
adopt wildcard option is added to the VCS command line as follows:
% vcs -adopt wildcard
% vcs -sverilog example.v -ad=example.init -adopt wildcard -full64
The use of the -adopt wildcard option and the "*" wildcard character in the
use_verilog command increases (sometimes almost doubles) the compilation
