The absolute path to the instance of the DUT that corresponds to the RAL model is
specified by defining the name_TOP_PATH symbol where name is the uppercase name of
the top-level block or system in the RAL model. Using the structure shown in Example 39,
S1_TOP_PATH the symbol must be defined to tb_top.dut, as shown below.
% vcs +define+S1_TOP_PATH=tb_top.dut \
ral_s1.sv
If the RALF specification contains arrays of system, block,regfile, register, or field
instances (see “Arrays and Register Files” for details on arrays of instances), the
hdl_path attribute must contain a %d, [%d], or [%g] format specifier.
Example 40 shows the key differences between them.
Example 40 A RALF Description Using Different Types of Array Backdoor
system s1 {
block b1[2] (b1_i%d) {
register r1 (dec.r1_reg) {
field f
}
}
block b2 (blk2) {
register r2[2] (r2_array[%d]) {
field f
}
}
block b3[2] (b3_gen_array[%g].blk) {
register r3 (dec.r3_reg) {
field f
}

}
}
%d Format Specifier
You should use the %d format specifier when the corresponding backdoor RTL
implementation of the RALF array is not really an array, rather a series of similarly named
non-array signals, for example, block b1 array in Example 40.
Example 41 shows that the generated backdoor path of such a RALF array does not have
any array in it.
Example 41 Generated Code During the %d Format Specifier Usage
class ral_reg_s1_b1_r1_bkdr extends uvm_ral_reg_backdoor;
int b1;

case (b1)
0:
Rw.value[0]= `S1_TOP_PATH.b1_i0.dec.r1_reg;;
1:
Rw.value[0]= `S1_TOP_PATH.b1_i1.dec.r1_reg;;

case (b1)
0: `S1_TOP_PATH.b1_i0.dec.r1_reg = rw.value[0];
1: `S1_TOP_PATH.b1_i1.dec.r1_reg = rw.value[0];
An example of the RTL implementation of a RALF array, which is not an array in the
backdoor or RTL, rather a series of similarly named non-array signals is as follows:
module s1();

b1 b1_i0();

b1 b1_i1();

endmodule
[%d] Format Specifier
You should use the [%d] format specifier only when the end signal/variable of the
corresponding backdoor RTL path/implementation is actually an array, but not a generated
instance array. For example, block r2 as shown in Example 40.
The advantage of having a normal array instead of generated instance array is that you
can access each array element by indexing with a variable as shown in Example 42.
Example 42 Generated Code During the [%d] Format Specifier Usage
class ral_reg_s1_b2_r2_bkdr extends uvm_ral_reg_backdoor;
int r2;

);
rw.value[0] = `S1_TOP_PATH.blk2.r2_array[r2];

`S1_TOP_PATH.blk2.r2_array[r2] = rw.value[0];
[%d:%d] Format Specifier
You can use the [%d:%d]format specifier to specify the register arrays modeled in RTL
using a single-dimension packed array in the UVM flow. Ralgen considers[%d:%d] as
an indication that the corresponding representation in RTL is of a packed register. It
generates the add_hdl_path as follows:
this.r[J].add_hdl_path('{
'{$psprintf("r[%0d:%0d]",
J*(size_of_register),
(J*size_of_register)+

(size_of_register-1)), -1, -1}
})
The backdoor paths are changed accordingly. Consider the following RALF code:
block bar {
register r[4] hdl_path=(r1[%d:%d]) {

backdoor_xor_mask 'hff

field f1 {
reset 0;
}

field f2[4] {
reset 0;
}
}
}
system foo {
block bar (bar);
}
For this, the XMR based backdoor paths are generated as follows:
case (r)
0: rw.value[0] = `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[0:7];
1: rw.value[0] = `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[8:15];
2: rw.value[0] = `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[16:23];
3: rw.value[0] = `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[24:31];

rw.value[0] = rw.value[0] ^ 'hff;

rw.value[0] = rw.value[0] ^ 'hff;
case (r)
0: `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[0:7] = rw.value[0];
1: `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[8:15] = rw.value[0];
2: `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[16:23] = rw.value[0];

3: `FOO_TOP_PATH.bar.r1[24:31] = rw.value[0];

The corresponding add_hdl_path is as follows:
this.r[J].add_hdl_path('{'{$psprintf("r1[%0d:%0d]", J*8, J*8+7), -1,
-1}});
[%g] Format Specifier
Use the [%g] format specifier when the corresponding backdoor RTL implementation of
the RALF array is a generated instance array. For example, block b3 array, as shown in
Example 43.
Since the generated instance array cannot be indexed using any variable,
numeric constants are used for indexing them.
Example 43 Generated Code During the [%g] Format specifier Usage
class ral_reg_s1_b3_r3_bkdr extends uvm_ral_reg_backdoor;
int b3;

