Create a platform access class for a CHIPit Platinum and Iridium systems from Synopsys.
Requires the VMM_HW_ARCH_CHIPIT compile-time symbol to be defined.
The name used to connect a message port to a message interface is the full HDL
path of the interface instance specified in the vmm_hw_arch::create_in_port() and

vmm_hw_arch::create_out_port() methods, less the top-level module name. The
optional user-specified interface name in vmm_hw_arch::create_in_port() and
vmm_hw_arch::create_out_port() is not used.
In CHIPit platforms, the links between vmm_hw_clock modules and their respective
vmm_hw_clock_control modules are established by assigning these modules to the same
clock domain (clock_num) in the RTL instantiation. The vmm_hw_arch::clock_control
function is only used to check that this connection is established in the hardware. If a
combination of clock module and clock control module is provided to this function which
are not assigned to the same clock domain in hardware, a ‘vmm_fatal error is generated.
