vmm_mam
This class is a memory allocation management utility class similar to C’s malloc() and
free(). A single instance of this class is used to manage a single, contiguous address
space. This memory allocation management class is used by any application-level process
that requires reserved space in the memory. The section of memory (called a region) will
remain reserved until it is explicitly released.
