vmm_sb_ds_typed::kind_e
Symbolic values for packet kind.
typedef enum {EITHER, INPUT, EXPECT} kind_e;
These symbols are used to specify the kind or purpose of a packet to the scoreboard
functionality.
vmm_sb_ds_typed::EITHER
Specifies that the direction of the packet is not relevant for the operation.
vmm_sb_ds_typed::INPUT
Specifies that the packet is an input packet going into the design under verification and a
corresponding response is to be expected.
vmm_sb_ds_typed::EXPECT
Specifies that the packet is an expected response packet coming out of the design under
verification and has been observed or is to be expected.
