txt2fsdb
txt2fsdb is a utility to transfer transactions or messages from a text file to an FSDB file

and set the relationship between transactions.

txt2fsdb txt_file [Options] or
txt2fsdb [Options] txt_file

-msg

Records messages to a log file. When the -msg option is
specified, logged messages are transferred from a text file
to an FSDB file, and the hierarchical tree of the specified
scope, stream variable, and attribute definitions are listed
under the created "msg_root" scope in the FSDB file.
Otherwise, txt2fsdb transfers transactions to an FSDB file.

-o fsdb_file

The name of the output file. Its default value is txt_file.fsdb.

