Specified in the design, the runtime variable can be passed as an argument.

reg [1023:0] suppressFile_reg = "suppress.list"; // reg string
string dumpListFile_string = "dump.list"; //string

$fsdbDumpMDAByFile("dump.list", "+fsdbfile+novas.fsdb");
$fsdbDumpMDAByFile(dumpListFile_reg);
$fsdbDumpMDAByFile(dumpListFile_string, option_reg);

Assertion Dumping Command
$fsdbDumpSVA
Dumps the SVA results to the FSDB file. The results of SVA assertions within the specified
scopes and/or modules can be dumped and saved to the same FSDB file that contains
dumped results for design signals or to a separate file.
$fsdbDumpSVA([ depth, | "level=",depth_var, ]
[instance | "instance=", instance_var ]
[ ,"option" | ,"option=",option_var ]*);

$fsdbDumpSVA;
$fsdbDumpSVA([depth] [, instance] [, "option"]*

call fsdbDumpSVA [depth] [instance] ["option"]*

Modelsim:
fsdbDumpSVA [depth] [instance] ["option"]*

Specify the levels of hierarchy to dump for the subsequent scopes.
"level="

Keyword to identify the next argument is a number.
depth_var

Specify how many levels of hierarchy to dump for the subsequent scopes in a variable.

Specify the instance name for which all SVA assertions below it are dumped.
"instance="

Keyword to identify the content of the next argument is a module scope or signal.
instance_var

This definition gives the module scope or signal represented by instance_var that
specifies the object to dump.

"+functions"

Enable dumping the SVA in functions in the
design.Example: $fsdbDumpSVA("+functions");

de"

mode means:
0: Disable functionality.
1 or 2: Skip all cell information.

"option="

Keyword to identify the next argument is a string.

Specify the option in a variable.
$fsdbDumpvars("+fsdbfile+1.fsdb");
$fsdbDumpSVA("+fsdbfile+1.fsdb");
#40 $fsdbDumpoff;
#40 $fsdbDumpon;
#10 $fsdbDumpFinish;
#30 $fsdbDumpfile("2.fsdb");
$fsdbDumpSVA(1,top);
//dump sva to 2.fsdb
#43 $finish;
end
$fsdbDumpSVA;

Dump all SVA assertions from design top and its descendants.
$fsdbDumpSVA(0, system);

Dump all SVA assertions under system and its descendants
$fsdbDumpSVA(1, system.arbiter);

Dump all SVA assertions under system.arbiter. The dumping level is set to 1, so dumping
excludes the SVA assertions under their descendant scopes.
$fsdbDumpvarsByFile("scope_lst.txt", "+fsdbfile=hdl.fsdb");
$fsdbDumpSVA(system.arbiter, "+fsdbfile=SVA.fsdb");

The first dumping command dumps design signals to the hdl.fsdb file. The second
dumping command dumps all SVA assertions under system.arbiter scope and its
descendants to the SVA.fsdb file.
For ModelSim users, the -sva and -assertdebug options should be specified in
the vsim command line options when dumping assertions. For example, > vsim
-c top -pli novas_fli.so -sva -assertdebug
The following is a code example for a vacuous success:
property P5;
@(posedge clk)
disable iff (rst)
(c) |=> (##[0:$] d);
endproperty : P5

If specified in the design, the design variable can be passed as an argument.
reg [255:0] depth_reg = 10;
