fsdbDumpvarsES
Dump signal-value-change information to the FSDB file for the signals in the specified
Essential Signal list which are within the specified scopes and levels.
LIMITATIONS:
Only hierarchical format for the Essential Signal list is supported. Multiple trees are
created in the FSDB file when multiple fsdbDumpvarsES system tasks are specified.
$fsdbDumpvarsES( depth, "instance", "es_list_file"[, "option,*"]);

The first three arguments depth, instance, and es_list_file are required. You can
place a delimiter in the instance argument to represent the design top.
For users of ModelSim, the delimiter between the hierarchical names is slash
(/).
For users of IUS, the delimiter is colon (:).
For example, fsdbDumpvarsES(0, ":", myeslist.txt, "+fsdbfile+dump.fsdb").
call fsdbDumpvarsES ESFileName
call fsdbDumpvarsES [instance] ESFileName
call fsdbDumpvarsES [depth] [instance] [option]* ESFileName

fsdbDumpvarsES ESFileName
fsdbDumpvarsES [instance] ESFileName
fsdbDumpvarsES [depth] [instance] [option]* ESFileName

